 "summary": "Validates the `inputs` option in the `sendall` RPC to reject duplicate outpoints. An `RPC_INVALID_PARAMETER` error is thrown immediately if the caller specifies the same UTXO more than once.",
 "problem": "When duplicate inputs are provided to `sendall`, the wallet counts their values multiple times and constructs a consensus-invalid transaction spending the same outpoint twice. The transaction fails mempool acceptance (`bad-txns-inputs-duplicate`), but is committed to the local wallet, locking the UTXOs and producing negative balance figures until the transaction is manually abandoned.",
 "evidence": [
  "Description provides a regtest reproduction where passing a single 1 BTC UTXO twice to `sendall` returns `complete: true`, builds an un-broadcastable transaction with an output for ~2 BTC rejected for `bad-txns-inputs-duplicate`, empties `listunspent`, and leaves `getbalances` reporting `nonmempool: -1.0`."
